        "original_id": "ee58d796-a975-556a-b982-f3f335c06bf4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ray Ruffels, Bob Hewitt, William Bowrey, Frew McMillan\n- Places: Sydney, South Africa\n- Events: 1969 Australian Open – Men's Singles\n- Topics: tennis, citizenship, doubles championships\n\nFacts:\n- Frew McMillan was born on 20 May 1942 and is a former professional male tennis player from South Africa.\n- Ray Ruffels was born on 23 March 1946 in Sydney and is an Australian former professional tennis player and coach.\n- In 1967, Bob Hewitt became a South African citizen after marrying a South African.\n- At the 1969 Australian Open – Men's Singles, defending champion William Bowrey lost in the quarterfinals to Ray Ruffels.\n- Frew McMillan won five major doubles championships, including three Wimbledon titles with Bob Hewitt.",
